{"id": "20560019", "revid": "753665", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20560019", "title": "Barbary Shore", "text": "Barbary Shore is Norman Mailer's second published novel, written after Mailer's great success with his 1948 debut \"The Naked and the Dead\". It concerns a protagonist who rents a room in a Brooklyn boarding house with the intention of writing a novel. Wounded during World War II, he is an amnesiac, and much of his past is a secret to him. After Rinehart &amp; Company published the novel in 1951, it received negative reviews and sold poorly. The failure of \"Barbary Shore\" and moderate success of Mailer's next novel, \"The Deer Park\" (1955) triggered a decade-long hiatus from the novel by Mailer, which ended with the publication of \"An American Dream\" in 1965."}
